{"name":"Rodeo","hex":"#7f5e46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rodeo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Contra Costa County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rodeo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rodeo","blocks":[{"text":"Rodeo is a competitive equestrian sport that arose out of the working practices of cattle herding in Spain and Mexico, expanding throughout the Americas and to other nations. It was originally based on the skills required of the working vaqueros and, later, cowboys in what today is the western United States, western Canada, and northern Mexico. Today, it is a sporting event that involves horses and other livestock, designed to test the skill and speed of the cowboys and cowgirls.\nProfessional rodeos generally comprise the following events: tie-down roping, team roping, steer wrestling, saddle bronc riding, bareback bronc riding, bull riding, breakaway roping, and barrel racing. The events are divided into two basic categories: the timed events and rough stock events. Depending on sanctioning organization and region, other events such as goat tying and pole bending may also be a part of some rodeos. The \"world's first public cowboy contest\" was held on July 4, 1883, in Pecos, Texas, between cattle driver Trav Windham and roper Morg Livingston."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/StampedeRodeo2002.JPG/330px-StampedeRodeo2002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rodeo","wikidata":"Q207703"},{"title":"Rodeo (Travis Scott album)","blocks":[{"text":"Rodeo is the debut studio album by American rapper Travis Scott. It was released on September 4, 2015, through Grand Hustle Records and distributed by Epic Records. The album features guest appearances from Quavo, Future, 2 Chainz, Juicy J, Kacy Hill, The Weeknd, Swae Lee, Chief Keef, Kanye West, Justin Bieber, Young Thug, Toro y Moi, and Schoolboy Q, while production was provided by Scott himself, alongside WondaGurl, Allen Ritter, Mike Dean, Metro Boomin, Frank Dukes, and Sonny Digital, among others."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/15/Travis_Scott_-_Rodeo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rodeo_(Travis_Scott_album)","wikidata":"Q20058669"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg/500px-Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg/1280px-Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg/500px-Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Branding calves, 1888","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACattle_branding_(Grabill_1888).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0f/Buffalo_Bill%E2%80%99s_Mexican_Vaqueros_Riding_Wild_Cattle.jpeg/500px-Buffalo_Bill%E2%80%99s_Mexican_Vaqueros_Riding_Wild_Cattle.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0f/Buffalo_Bill%E2%80%99s_Mexican_Vaqueros_Riding_Wild_Cattle.jpeg/1280px-Buffalo_Bill%E2%80%99s_Mexican_Vaqueros_Riding_Wild_Cattle.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0f/Buffalo_Bill%E2%80%99s_Mexican_Vaqueros_Riding_Wild_Cattle.jpeg/500px-Buffalo_Bill%E2%80%99s_Mexican_Vaqueros_Riding_Wild_Cattle.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org